16165.sol:
Using mirror formula, $\frac{1}{f}=\frac{1}{u}+\frac{1}{v}$
or, $\frac{-1}{f}=\frac{-1}{u}+\frac{1}{v}[\therefore \mathrm{u} \ \text{$ and $} \mathrm{f}$ negative for concave mirror
$\begin{aligned}
& \Rightarrow \frac{1}{v}=\frac{1}{u}-\frac{1}{f} \Rightarrow \frac{1}{v}=\frac{f-u}{u f} \\
& v=\frac{u f}{u-f}
\end{aligned}$
Length of image,
$\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{L}=|v|-|f|=v=\frac{u f}{u-f}-f \\
& \mathrm{ L}=\frac{u f-f(u-f)}{u-f} \\
& =\frac{u f-u f+f^2}{u-f}=\frac{f^2}{u-f}
\end{aligned}$

